WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.369 --> 00:00:02.041
- [Narrator] They say
money can't buy happiness,

00:00:02.041 --> 00:00:03.318
but can it buy friendship?

00:00:03.318 --> 00:00:05.872
In order to find answers, I
posted an ad on Craigslist

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:08.647
seeking someone that I
would pay to be my BFF,

00:00:08.647 --> 00:00:11.027
while testing their skills
as the ultimate friend.

00:00:11.027 --> 00:00:14.997
This is the story of how I
bought a friend off Craigslist.

00:00:14.997 --> 00:00:18.248
- I am being paid to be
somebody's best friend.

00:00:18.248 --> 00:00:20.385
Seems interesting, I guess.

00:00:20.385 --> 00:00:21.662
- Thank you for coming.

00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:22.788
I'm excited.

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:26.596
My hope is that even though I'm
buying your friendship today

00:00:26.596 --> 00:00:27.757
that that's just an investment,

00:00:27.757 --> 00:00:30.520
and that'll be as
valuable, if not more so,

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.389
than a real, genuine friendship.

00:00:32.389 --> 00:00:33.875
- Yeah, no, same.

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:35.315
- Do you think you're a good friend?

00:00:35.315 --> 00:00:36.534
- I would say so, yeah.

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:37.440
I hope so.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.810
- Why do you think you'll be a good friend

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.226
to me, specifically?

00:00:40.226 --> 00:00:41.329
- I'm very blunt.

00:00:41.329 --> 00:00:43.442
If you're doing something
weird with somebody

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:47.366
and I'm like, "oh, man,
like, chill, don't do that."

00:00:47.366 --> 00:00:50.048
- As your friend, I'm going to look out

00:00:50.048 --> 00:00:51.406
for your best needs.

00:00:51.406 --> 00:00:52.239
- Aww.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:53.502
- I'm going to show you
love, and I want you

00:00:53.502 --> 00:00:54.570
to show me love.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:55.403
- Okay.

00:00:55.403 --> 00:00:56.381
- Do you think you're up for the task?

00:00:56.381 --> 00:00:59.121
- I, yeah, I think I'm up for this task.

00:00:59.121 --> 00:01:01.002
- There are many variables
when it comes to friendship,

00:01:01.002 --> 00:01:04.043
but I want to highlight three
very important things to me.

00:01:04.043 --> 00:01:04.876
- Yeah.

00:01:04.876 --> 00:01:05.709
- Loyalty.

00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:08.298
I don't want you sleeping
with anyone I'm dating.

00:01:08.298 --> 00:01:09.131
- Yeah.

00:01:09.131 --> 00:01:10.818
- I don't want you coming after my family.

00:01:10.818 --> 00:01:12.269
Secondly, honesty.

00:01:12.269 --> 00:01:14.417
I tell you you look good in
a shirt, I'm being honest.

00:01:14.417 --> 00:01:15.508
What did you say, Ahmed?

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:16.948
- I said, "That's a nice shirt."

00:01:16.948 --> 00:01:18.062
- It's great, $24.99.

00:01:18.062 --> 00:01:18.895
- [Ahmed] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:18.895 --> 00:01:19.728
- Great value.

00:01:19.728 --> 00:01:21.150
Lastly, I want you to stand up for me.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:21.983
- [Ahmed] Yeah.

00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:24.738
- Okay, if someone's coming
up and wants to stab me,

00:01:24.738 --> 00:01:26.863
I expect you to take the knife.

00:01:26.863 --> 00:01:28.604
- If we accidentally do kill him,

00:01:28.604 --> 00:01:29.951
we're hiding that murder, though.

00:01:29.951 --> 00:01:31.565
- If we kill someone, are
reporting it to the police

00:01:31.565 --> 00:01:33.596
because it is against the
law to murder someone.

00:01:33.596 --> 00:01:34.429
- Right.

00:01:34.429 --> 00:01:35.442
- [Narrator] Did Ahmed
even have what it takes

00:01:35.442 --> 00:01:37.172
to be my best friend?

00:01:37.172 --> 00:01:39.163
I decided to get to
know him a little better

00:01:39.163 --> 00:01:40.812
before I tested his skills.

00:01:40.812 --> 00:01:41.926
- What's your favorite holiday?

00:01:41.926 --> 00:01:44.736
- Well, my family's Muslim,
so we have a Big Eid

00:01:44.736 --> 00:01:45.908
and a Small Eid.

00:01:45.908 --> 00:01:46.741
- Oh.

00:01:46.741 --> 00:01:47.929
- They're both pretty poppin'.

00:01:47.929 --> 00:01:49.008
How about you, what's your--?

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:50.343
- I love Christmas.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.609
- Yeah, that's a classic.

00:01:51.609 --> 00:01:53.513
- I feel people are just generally kinder

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.465
during the holidays.

00:01:54.465 --> 00:01:55.429
What's the most embarrassing thing

00:01:55.429 --> 00:01:56.508
that happened to you in college?

00:01:56.508 --> 00:01:57.341
- One time,

00:01:57.341 --> 00:01:58.174
(chuckles)

00:01:58.174 --> 00:02:00.723
I got all my food in the dining hall,

00:02:00.723 --> 00:02:02.859
and I trip over a flat surface,

00:02:02.859 --> 00:02:04.101
- Oh, God.

00:02:04.101 --> 00:02:07.062
- And I spilled everywhere,
and I'm on the ground,

00:02:07.062 --> 00:02:09.860
food everywhere after
I just finished paying.

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.508
- [Narrator] Ahmed seemed to be fun,

00:02:11.508 --> 00:02:14.910
but I still wasn't convinced
he was best friend material.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.801
Friendship is about good
times and bad times.

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:19.531
My first test for Ahmed was to see

00:02:19.531 --> 00:02:22.050
if he could be vulnerable with me.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:26.717
My last serious relationship
was about two years ago.

00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:29.237
The thing that sticks to
me about that relationship

00:02:29.237 --> 00:02:30.070
is the way it ended.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:31.919
It didn't end in some dramatic blowout,

00:02:31.919 --> 00:02:34.101
there was no screaming or yelling,

00:02:34.101 --> 00:02:37.601
it just, life happened, and it just ended.

00:02:39.755 --> 00:02:43.680
You spend two years with
someone, and it's just--

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.350
sometimes it's just, it's sad to look back

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.740
and think about what could have been.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.737
- That's the way life goes, you know?

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.281
Things that bring you down can bring you

00:02:53.281 --> 00:02:54.639
to a different direction.

00:02:54.639 --> 00:02:55.661
- Here's to that.

00:02:55.661 --> 00:02:56.834
- Here's to that.

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.912
- How about you, do you have
anything you wanna share?

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.607
- All right, there was
a hard time in my life

00:03:00.607 --> 00:03:03.274
where I was a junior in college.

00:03:04.206 --> 00:03:07.991
In my family, there's a lot of
pressure to get good grades,

00:03:07.991 --> 00:03:09.663
and to do well in school.

00:03:09.663 --> 00:03:12.345
And I was supposed to do
this fast-track program

00:03:12.345 --> 00:03:13.633
that my university had.

00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:15.804
I had studied, and I'd
taken practice tests,

00:03:15.804 --> 00:03:18.266
and you have score a 650.

00:03:18.266 --> 00:03:20.843
And at the same time, I was
also applying to be an RA.

00:03:20.843 --> 00:03:24.605
I took the test and had
my final interview for RA

00:03:24.605 --> 00:03:27.275
all in the same week,
so I finished the exam

00:03:27.275 --> 00:03:28.692
and scored a 540.

00:03:30.027 --> 00:03:32.116
Later that evening, I'd
found out I got rejected

00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:34.020
from the RA program as well.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.180
I had called my mom right afterwards

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.119
to tell her both bad news
at the same time, I guess,

00:03:38.119 --> 00:03:40.255
to kind of like rip the Band-Aid off,

00:03:40.255 --> 00:03:43.668
and she didn't know this,
but I was low-key crying

00:03:43.668 --> 00:03:46.722
on the phone, and I was
holding the phone away from me

00:03:46.722 --> 00:03:48.626
because it was hurting so much.

00:03:48.626 --> 00:03:50.414
So I was like, "God damn."

00:03:50.414 --> 00:03:51.714
I just screwed up big.

00:03:51.714 --> 00:03:54.315
- Some things just don't
happen for a reason,

00:03:54.315 --> 00:03:58.343
and then sometimes
better things will come.

00:03:58.343 --> 00:04:00.793
- [Narrator] For the next test,
I organized for a co-worker

00:04:00.793 --> 00:04:03.475
to run into our set and start bullying me.

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:07.642
My hope was that Ahmed would
step up and defend my honor.

00:04:08.525 --> 00:04:09.605
- Oh, shit.
- Like at bars, or something.

00:04:09.605 --> 00:04:11.059
- Could you tell me a story
about one of those times?

00:04:11.059 --> 00:04:12.104
- Yeah...

00:04:12.104 --> 00:04:14.217
- Hey, did you hear the news?

00:04:14.217 --> 00:04:15.331
- Uh, no.

00:04:15.331 --> 00:04:16.945
- Someone told me about your video idea.

00:04:16.945 --> 00:04:18.187
I think it's awful.

00:04:18.187 --> 00:04:19.035
- He just came out of nowhere.

00:04:19.035 --> 00:04:22.576
I was actually genuinely
unsure what that was.

00:04:22.576 --> 00:04:24.073
- [Bully] I'm sorry, man.

00:04:24.073 --> 00:04:25.275
I'm actually not that sorry.

00:04:25.275 --> 00:04:27.393
- [Narrator] I waited for
Ahmed with baited breath.

00:04:27.393 --> 00:04:28.763
If he couldn't stand up for me,

00:04:28.763 --> 00:04:32.536
our entire friendship could crumble.

00:04:32.536 --> 00:04:35.927
- Wow, hold on, this is my
friend you're talking to,

00:04:35.927 --> 00:04:39.010
so if you could not, that'd be great.

00:04:40.164 --> 00:04:42.684
He is my friend for life, right here.

00:04:42.684 --> 00:04:45.702
And he's a great person, and
his video idea was phenomenal,

00:04:45.702 --> 00:04:47.989
because look how great of friends we are.

00:04:47.989 --> 00:04:50.149
I was like, I don't think
this kid's gonna pull a knife,

00:04:50.149 --> 00:04:53.191
but I was like, pretty
close, pretty close,

00:04:53.191 --> 00:04:54.735
he's getting oddly aggressive.

00:04:54.735 --> 00:04:58.450
- What you did just now,
I'm never gonna forget that.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:04:59.283
- Of course.
- You know what?

00:04:59.283 --> 00:05:00.911
- I mean, that's pretty--

00:05:00.911 --> 00:05:03.119
- [Narrator] I decided to
send him on one final mission

00:05:03.119 --> 00:05:04.628
to determine it all.

00:05:04.628 --> 00:05:07.728
I wanted Ahmed to know me well
enough on a best friend level

00:05:07.728 --> 00:05:10.468
to buy me a personalized gift.

00:05:10.468 --> 00:05:14.551
(uplifting, inspirational music)

00:05:17.631 --> 00:05:19.673
- Earlier today, we talked
about the tryout friend.

00:05:19.673 --> 00:05:23.133
Honesty, loyalty, and
whether or not you stand up

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.085
for your friends.

00:05:24.085 --> 00:05:28.520
I will be evaluating you
on those three qualities.

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:31.097
When it came to honesty, we
had a very intimate moment

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.965
in the pop-up park, and I
genuinely was very moved

00:05:33.965 --> 00:05:36.194
by the story you told about
the hardship you went through

00:05:36.194 --> 00:05:38.191
in college, because we
connected on a level

00:05:38.191 --> 00:05:40.444
that not a lot of friends do.

00:05:40.444 --> 00:05:42.324
You gave me an A+.

00:05:42.324 --> 00:05:43.950
- Yeah!

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:45.401
Yes, right here.

00:05:45.401 --> 00:05:46.783
All right, that's all right.

00:05:46.783 --> 00:05:48.582
- Still more to come.
- Okay, all right.

00:05:48.582 --> 00:05:49.534
- Loyalty.

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:52.843
Loyalty is a very important
trait in a relationship.

00:05:52.843 --> 00:05:56.581
And today, we built
loyalty through the times

00:05:56.581 --> 00:05:57.986
we shared together.

00:05:57.986 --> 00:05:59.972
I will give you a B+.

00:05:59.972 --> 00:06:01.295
- I'll take it, I'll take it.

00:06:01.295 --> 00:06:03.640
- Standing up for each other.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:06.009
Today, I was viciously attacked.

00:06:06.009 --> 00:06:10.304
He attacked me with his words
for a good solid 15 seconds

00:06:10.304 --> 00:06:11.918
before you said anything.

00:06:11.918 --> 00:06:14.449
So for that, I will give you an A-.

00:06:14.449 --> 00:06:15.866
- Okay, wow, woo.

00:06:16.783 --> 00:06:19.859
- I believe the last thing
that I can evaluate you on

00:06:19.859 --> 00:06:22.356
is the gift that you bought me.

00:06:22.356 --> 00:06:23.189
- That's true.

00:06:23.189 --> 00:06:24.022
- Should you close your eyes?
- Should I close my eyes?

00:06:24.022 --> 00:06:25.005
- Yeah, close your eyes.
- I need to close my eyes.

00:06:25.005 --> 00:06:26.662
- Close your eyes, okay.

00:06:26.662 --> 00:06:27.533
All righty.

00:06:27.533 --> 00:06:29.205
Open them up.

00:06:29.205 --> 00:06:31.399
You said you love Christmas so much,

00:06:31.399 --> 00:06:33.164
I decided to bring Christmas to you.

00:06:33.164 --> 00:06:34.778
- Oh my God!

00:06:34.778 --> 00:06:35.611
Ahmed!

00:06:35.611 --> 00:06:37.216
You shouldn't have!

00:06:37.216 --> 00:06:38.674
- I had to.

00:06:38.674 --> 00:06:39.882
(laughing)

00:06:39.882 --> 00:06:41.670
You are very passionate about Christmas,

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.189
and I saw that in the
store, and just knew it.

00:06:44.189 --> 00:06:47.118
- I think that when people
hear that I was paying you

00:06:47.118 --> 00:06:48.058
to be my best friend for a day,

00:06:48.058 --> 00:06:49.683
they probably thought I was crazy.

00:06:49.683 --> 00:06:51.483
But I honestly think that today,

00:06:51.483 --> 00:06:53.190
we've built a good chemistry.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.813
I think that there is something here,

00:06:55.813 --> 00:06:58.460
and I don't know what
you're doing this weekend,

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.690
but Friday I'm going to a Halloween party.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:01.523
- Are you?

00:07:01.523 --> 00:07:03.244
- Yes, if you would like to come with.

00:07:03.244 --> 00:07:04.149
- You know what?

00:07:04.149 --> 00:07:05.357
That sounds like a plan.

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:07.748
- Now just to make it clear,
on Friday, when we hang out

00:07:07.748 --> 00:07:11.371
as friends, I will not be paying you.

00:07:11.371 --> 00:07:12.532
- I'm very excited.

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:15.423
- Ahmed was the best
friend I could've paid for.

00:07:15.423 --> 00:07:19.428
We even did a best friend
photo shoot to end the day.

00:07:19.428 --> 00:07:22.040
He was truly someone I'll never forget.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.670
- If we had met at a house
party or something like that,

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.503
there's no doubt we
would've ended up talking

00:07:27.503 --> 00:07:29.023
and talking about all this random--

00:07:29.023 --> 00:07:29.856
(beeps)

00:07:29.856 --> 00:07:30.886
that we both like.

00:07:30.886 --> 00:07:34.136
(bright, bouncy music)

00:07:41.823 --> 00:07:42.972
(whooshing)

00:07:42.972 --> 00:07:44.238
(squeaking)

